<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Locating specific entries a_{ij} in a matrix using row and column indices</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the \({@m@} \times {@n@}\) matrix</p>
<p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.15em;">\[ A = {@MM@}. \]</p>
<p>The entry \(a_{ij}\) is the number in <b>row \(i\)</b> and <b>column \(j\)</b>. Find the following entries. <i>(Note: Enter each entry as a single integer, such as <code>-15</code> or <code>14</code>.)</i></p>
<p>\( a_{ {@i1@}{@j1@} } = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\( a_{ {@i2@}{@j2@} } = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\( a_{ {@i3@}{@j3@} } = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>In matrix notation \(a_{ij}\), the <b>first subscript \(i\)</b> gives the <b>row number</b> (counting from top to bottom) and the <b>second subscript \(j\)</b> gives the <b>column number</b> (counting from left to right).</p>

<p><b>1. Finding \(a_{ {@i1@}{@j1@} }\):</b><br>
Move down to <b>row \({@i1@}\)</b> and across to <b>column \({@j1@}\)</b>, which gives \({@ta1@}\).</p>

<p><b>2. Finding \(a_{ {@i2@}{@j2@} }\):</b><br>
Move down to <b>row \({@i2@}\)</b> and across to <b>column \({@j2@}\)</b>, which gives \({@ta2@}\).</p>

<p><b>3. Finding \(a_{ {@i3@}{@j3@} }\):</b><br>
Move down to <b>row \({@i3@}\)</b> and across to <b>column \({@j3@}\)</b>, which gives \({@ta3@}\).</p>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.15em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ a_{ {@i1@}{@j1@} } = {@ta1@}, \quad a_{ {@i2@}{@j2@} } = {@ta2@}, \quad a_{ {@i3@}{@j3@} } = {@ta3@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
